IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bgg4-nouns`

-- bgg4-appealable: BGG 4. Kapitel, 1. Abschnitt, Anfechtbare Entscheide (Art. 90 to 94).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively; nobody's point of view.
--
-- Every decision function here answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes to the case, in its own words;
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no to the case, in its own words
--               (a branch tagged  FALSE-kind  names the words);
--   NOTHING     not covered (a branch tagged  NOTHING-kind  says why).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Same conventions as the chapter 3 modules (see bgg3-civil): a failed "wenn" inside a
-- limb is JUST FALSE (reading (a), for a lawyer); a grant limited by its own wording
-- whose case falls outside the limit is NOTHING.
-- The English identifiers are glosses of the German; the quoted lines are the text.

§ `Art 90 Endentscheide (final decisions)`

-- src:11 | Die Beschwerde ist zulässig gegen Entscheide, die das Verfahren abschliessen.
@ref Art. 90 BGG (src:11)
GIVEN `the decision ends the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN              -- Entscheid, der das Verfahren abschliesst
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 90 the appeal is admissible against the decision` MEANS
    IF `the decision ends the proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant reaches only "Entscheide, die das Verfahren abschliessen"; a decision that does not end the proceedings is dealt with by Art 91 to 93 and this Article does not say no to it

§ `Art 91 Teilentscheide (partial decisions)`

-- src:14 | Die Beschwerde ist zulässig gegen einen Entscheid, der:
-- src:15 | a. nur einen Teil der gestellten Begehren behandelt, wenn diese Begehren unabhängig von den anderen beurteilt werden können;
@ref Art. 91(a) BGG (src:14-15)
GIVEN `the decision deals with only some of the claims made` IS A BOOLEAN        -- nur einen Teil der gestellten Begehren
      `those claims can be judged independently of the others` IS A BOOLEAN      -- unabhängig von den anderen beurteilt werden können
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 91(a) the appeal is admissible against the decision that deals with only some of the claims` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the decision deals with only some of the claims made` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): limb (a) reaches only a decision that "nur einen Teil der gestellten Begehren behandelt"
        IF `those claims can be judged independently of the others` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "wenn diese Begehren unabhängig von den anderen beurteilt werden können" (a failed "wenn": reading (a), for a lawyer; fork F1)

-- src:14 | Die Beschwerde ist zulässig gegen einen Entscheid, der:
-- src:16 | b. das Verfahren nur für einen Teil der Streitgenossen und Streitgenossinnen abschliesst.
@ref Art. 91(b) BGG (src:14) (src:16)
GIVEN `the decision ends the proceedings for only some of the joint litigants` IS A BOOLEAN   -- für einen Teil der Streitgenossen und Streitgenossinnen
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 91(b) the appeal is admissible against the decision that ends the proceedings for only some of the joint litigants` MEANS
    IF `the decision ends the proceedings for only some of the joint litigants`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): limb (b) reaches only a decision that "das Verfahren nur für einen Teil der Streitgenossen und Streitgenossinnen abschliesst"

-- src:14 | Die Beschwerde ist zulässig gegen einen Entscheid, der:
-- src:15 | a. nur einen Teil der gestellten Begehren behandelt, wenn diese Begehren unabhängig von den anderen beurteilt werden können;
-- src:16 | b. das Verfahren nur für einen Teil der Streitgenossen und Streitgenossinnen abschliesst.
@ref Art. 91 BGG (src:14-16)
GIVEN `the decision deals with only some of the claims made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those claims can be judged independently of the others` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision ends the proceedings for only some of the joint litigants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 91 the appeal is admissible against the partial decision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 91(a) the appeal is admissible against the decision that deals with only some of the claims` `the decision deals with only some of the claims made` `those claims can be judged independently of the others`)
            OR fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 91(b) the appeal is admissible against the decision that ends the proceedings for only some of the joint litigants` `the decision ends the proceedings for only some of the joint litigants`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `Art 91(a) the appeal is admissible against the decision that deals with only some of the claims` `the decision deals with only some of the claims made` `those claims can be judged independently of the others` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE          -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "wenn diese Begehren unabhängig von den anderen beurteilt werden können" (limb (a) is the only route for a decision on only some of the claims and its "wenn" failed; limb (b) does not hold: reading (a), for a lawyer; fork F1)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "ist zulässig gegen einen Entscheid, der: a. ...; b. ..." names two kinds of decision and does not close the list with "nur"; a decision of neither kind is not said to be inadmissible by this Article

§ `Art 92 Vor- und Zwischenentscheide über die Zuständigkeit und den Ausstand (preliminary and interlocutory decisions on jurisdiction and recusal)`

-- src:19 | 1 Gegen selbständig eröffnete Vor- und Zwischenentscheide über die Zuständigkeit und über Ausstandsbegehren ist die Beschwerde zulässig.
@ref Art. 92(1) BGG (src:19)
GIVEN `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` IS A BOOLEAN       -- Vor- oder Zwischenentscheid
      `the decision was notified independently` IS A BOOLEAN                       -- selbständig eröffnet
      `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` IS A BOOLEAN   -- über die Zuständigkeit und über Ausstandsbegehren
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 92(1) the appeal is admissible against the preliminary or interlocutory decision on jurisdiction or recusal` MEANS
    IF `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` AND `the decision was notified independently` AND `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant reaches only "selbständig eröffnete Vor- und Zwischenentscheide über die Zuständigkeit und über Ausstandsbegehren"; any other decision is dealt with by Art 90, 91 and 93

-- src:20 | 2 Diese Entscheide können später nicht mehr angefochten werden.
@ref Art. 92(2) BGG (src:20)
GIVEN `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision was notified independently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 92(2) the decision can be challenged later` MEANS
    IF fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 92(1) the appeal is admissible against the preliminary or interlocutory decision on jurisdiction or recusal` `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` `the decision was notified independently` `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal`)
    THEN JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Diese Entscheide können später nicht mehr angefochten werden." ("Diese Entscheide" are the decisions of paragraph 1)
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative reaches only "diese Entscheide", the decisions of paragraph 1; for any other decision the sentence is silent

§ `Art 93 Andere Vor- und Zwischenentscheide (other preliminary and interlocutory decisions)`

-- src:23 | 1 Gegen andere selbständig eröffnete Vor- und Zwischenentscheide ist die Beschwerde zulässig:
-- src:24 | a. wenn sie einen nicht wieder gutzumachenden Nachteil bewirken können; oder
@ref Art. 93(1)(a) BGG (src:23-24)
GIVEN `the decision may cause irreparable harm` IS A BOOLEAN      -- einen nicht wieder gutzumachenden Nachteil bewirken können: an open-textured judgment, asked as a fact
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 93(1)(a) the appeal is admissible because the decision may cause irreparable harm` MEANS
    IF `the decision may cause irreparable harm`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "wenn sie einen nicht wieder gutzumachenden Nachteil bewirken können" (a failed "wenn": reading (a), for a lawyer; fork F2)

-- src:23 | 1 Gegen andere selbständig eröffnete Vor- und Zwischenentscheide ist die Beschwerde zulässig:
-- src:25 | b. wenn die Gutheissung der Beschwerde sofort einen Endentscheid herbeiführen und damit einen bedeutenden Aufwand an Zeit oder Kosten für ein weitläufiges Beweisverfahren ersparen würde.
@ref Art. 93(1)(b) BGG (src:23) (src:25)
GIVEN `allowing the appeal would immediately bring about a final decision` IS A BOOLEAN                   -- sofort einen Endentscheid herbeiführen
      `that would spare a significant expenditure of time or cost for a lengthy evidentiary procedure` IS A BOOLEAN   -- bedeutenden Aufwand an Zeit oder Kosten für ein weitläufiges Beweisverfahren ersparen
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 93(1)(b) the appeal is admissible because allowing it would immediately bring about a final decision` MEANS
    IF `allowing the appeal would immediately bring about a final decision` AND `that would spare a significant expenditure of time or cost for a lengthy evidentiary procedure`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "wenn die Gutheissung der Beschwerde sofort einen Endentscheid herbeiführen und damit einen bedeutenden Aufwand an Zeit oder Kosten für ein weitläufiges Beweisverfahren ersparen würde" (a failed "wenn": reading (a), for a lawyer; fork F2)

-- src:23 | 1 Gegen andere selbständig eröffnete Vor- und Zwischenentscheide ist die Beschwerde zulässig:
-- src:24 | a. wenn sie einen nicht wieder gutzumachenden Nachteil bewirken können; oder
-- src:25 | b. wenn die Gutheissung der Beschwerde sofort einen Endentscheid herbeiführen und damit einen bedeutenden Aufwand an Zeit oder Kosten für ein weitläufiges Beweisverfahren ersparen würde.
@ref Art. 93(1) BGG (src:23-25)
GIVEN `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision was notified independently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision may cause irreparable harm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `allowing the appeal would immediately bring about a final decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that would spare a significant expenditure of time or cost for a lengthy evidentiary procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 93(1) the appeal is admissible against the other preliminary or interlocutory decision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` AND `the decision was notified independently` AND (NOT `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal`)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph reaches only "andere selbständig eröffnete Vor- und Zwischenentscheide", other than those of Art 92
        IF     fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 93(1)(a) the appeal is admissible because the decision may cause irreparable harm` `the decision may cause irreparable harm`)
            OR fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 93(1)(b) the appeal is admissible because allowing it would immediately bring about a final decision` `allowing the appeal would immediately bring about a final decision` `that would spare a significant expenditure of time or cost for a lengthy evidentiary procedure`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ist die Beschwerde zulässig: a. wenn ...; oder b. wenn ..." and neither "wenn" holds (the provision's own question, in the manner of the "no saving on these facts" reading of chapter 3 fork F2: reading (a), for a lawyer; fork F2)

-- src:26 | 2 Auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen und dem Gebiet des Asyls sind Vor- und Zwischenentscheide nicht anfechtbar.[^1] Vorbehalten bleiben Beschwerden gegen Entscheide über die Auslieferungshaft sowie über die Beschlagnahme von Vermögenswerten und Wertgegenständen, sofern die Voraussetzungen von Absatz 1 erfüllt sind.
@ref Art. 93(2) BGG (src:26)
GIVEN `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN   -- Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen
      `the matter is in the field of asylum` IS A BOOLEAN                                                -- Gebiet des Asyls
      `the decision is on extradition detention` IS A BOOLEAN                                            -- Entscheid über die Auslieferungshaft
      `the decision is on the seizure of assets or valuables` IS A BOOLEAN                               -- Beschlagnahme von Vermögenswerten und Wertgegenständen
      `the decision was notified independently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision may cause irreparable harm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `allowing the appeal would immediately bring about a final decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that would spare a significant expenditure of time or cost for a lengthy evidentiary procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 93(2) the appeal is admissible against the preliminary or interlocutory decision in the field` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of "Vor- und Zwischenentscheide" only
        IF NOT (`the matter is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` OR `the matter is in the field of asylum`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen und dem Gebiet des Asyls": other fields are outside the paragraph
        IF     (`the decision is on extradition detention` OR `the decision is on the seizure of assets or valuables`)
           AND fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 93(1) the appeal is admissible against the other preliminary or interlocutory decision` `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` `the decision was notified independently` `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` `the decision may cause irreparable harm` `allowing the appeal would immediately bring about a final decision` `that would spare a significant expenditure of time or cost for a lengthy evidentiary procedure`)
        THEN JUST TRUE          -- the reservation: "Vorbehalten bleiben Beschwerden gegen Entscheide über die Auslieferungshaft sowie über die Beschlagnahme von Vermögenswerten und Wertgegenständen, sofern die Voraussetzungen von Absatz 1 erfüllt sind."
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "sind Vor- und Zwischenentscheide nicht anfechtbar" (a flat negative; the reservation lifts it only where the decision is on extradition detention or seizure "sofern die Voraussetzungen von Absatz 1 erfüllt sind")

-- src:27 | 3 Ist die Beschwerde nach den Absätzen 1 und 2 nicht zulässig oder wurde von ihr kein Gebrauch gemacht, so sind die betreffenden Vor- und Zwischenentscheide durch Beschwerde gegen den Endentscheid anfechtbar, soweit sie sich auf dessen Inhalt auswirken.
@ref Art. 93(3) BGG (src:27)
GIVEN `the decision is another preliminary or interlocutory decision, not one on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal against it under paragraphs 1 and 2 is not admissible` IS A BOOLEAN        -- die Beschwerde nach den Absätzen 1 und 2 nicht zulässig
      `no use was made of the appeal against it under paragraphs 1 and 2` IS A BOOLEAN       -- von ihr kein Gebrauch gemacht
      `the decision affects the content of the final decision` IS A BOOLEAN                   -- sich auf dessen Inhalt auswirken
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 93(3) the preliminary or interlocutory decision can be challenged by the appeal against the final decision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the decision is another preliminary or interlocutory decision, not one on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "die betreffenden Vor- und Zwischenentscheide" are those of paragraphs 1 and 2, not the decisions of Art 92 (which Art 92(2) says cannot be challenged later)
        IF NOT (`the appeal against it under paragraphs 1 and 2 is not admissible` OR `no use was made of the appeal against it under paragraphs 1 and 2`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Ist die Beschwerde nach den Absätzen 1 und 2 nicht zulässig oder wurde von ihr kein Gebrauch gemacht, so sind ... anfechtbar" (a failed "Ist ..., so": reading (a), for a lawyer; fork F3)
        IF `the decision affects the content of the final decision` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "anfechtbar, soweit sie sich auf dessen Inhalt auswirken": to the extent they do not affect the content the text grants nothing and says no to nothing (fork F3)

§ `Art 94 Rechtsverweigerung und Rechtsverzögerung (denial and delay of justice)`

-- src:30 | Gegen das unrechtmässige Verweigern oder Verzögern eines anfechtbaren Entscheids kann Beschwerde geführt werden.
@ref Art. 94 BGG (src:30)
GIVEN `the authority refused or delayed a decision` IS A BOOLEAN                         -- Verweigern oder Verzögern
      `the refusal or delay is unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN                                    -- unrechtmässig: an open-textured judgment, asked as a fact
      `the decision refused or delayed is one that can be appealed` IS A BOOLEAN         -- anfechtbarer Entscheid
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 94 the appeal lies against the unlawful refusal or delay of a decision` MEANS
    IF `the authority refused or delayed a decision` AND `the refusal or delay is unlawful` AND `the decision refused or delayed is one that can be appealed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Gegen das unrechtmässige Verweigern oder Verzögern eines anfechtbaren Entscheids kann Beschwerde geführt werden" grants an appeal in that case and says no to no other

§ `Arts 90 to 93 taken together (the section's kinds of decision)`

-- The section as a whole.  Art 90 (decisions that end the proceedings), Art 91 (partial
-- decisions), Art 92(1) (preliminary decisions on jurisdiction and recusal) and Art 93 (other
-- preliminary decisions) name the kinds of decision that can be appealed; this function takes
-- the facts of all four.  It gathers the per-section answers by the rule: a grant that says
-- yes gives JUST TRUE; Art 93(2), the more specific rule for two fields, answers for a
-- preliminary decision in those fields; otherwise Art 93(1)'s answer stands (fork F4).
-- src:11 | Die Beschwerde ist zulässig gegen Entscheide, die das Verfahren abschliessen.
-- src:14 | Die Beschwerde ist zulässig gegen einen Entscheid, der:
-- src:15 | a. nur einen Teil der gestellten Begehren behandelt, wenn diese Begehren unabhängig von den anderen beurteilt werden können;
-- src:16 | b. das Verfahren nur für einen Teil der Streitgenossen und Streitgenossinnen abschliesst.
-- src:19 | 1 Gegen selbständig eröffnete Vor- und Zwischenentscheide über die Zuständigkeit und über Ausstandsbegehren ist die Beschwerde zulässig.
-- src:23 | 1 Gegen andere selbständig eröffnete Vor- und Zwischenentscheide ist die Beschwerde zulässig:
-- src:24 | a. wenn sie einen nicht wieder gutzumachenden Nachteil bewirken können; oder
-- src:25 | b. wenn die Gutheissung der Beschwerde sofort einen Endentscheid herbeiführen und damit einen bedeutenden Aufwand an Zeit oder Kosten für ein weitläufiges Beweisverfahren ersparen würde.
-- src:26 | 2 Auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen und dem Gebiet des Asyls sind Vor- und Zwischenentscheide nicht anfechtbar.[^1] Vorbehalten bleiben Beschwerden gegen Entscheide über die Auslieferungshaft sowie über die Beschlagnahme von Vermögenswerten und Wertgegenständen, sofern die Voraussetzungen von Absatz 1 erfüllt sind.
@ref Art. 90 to 93 BGG (src:11) (src:14-16) (src:19) (src:23-26)
GIVEN `the decision ends the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision deals with only some of the claims made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those claims can be judged independently of the others` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision ends the proceedings for only some of the joint litigants` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision was notified independently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is in the field of asylum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is on extradition detention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is on the seizure of assets or valuables` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision may cause irreparable harm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `allowing the appeal would immediately bring about a final decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that would spare a significant expenditure of time or cost for a lengthy evidentiary procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against the decision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 90 answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `Art 91 answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `Art 92(1) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `Art 93(2) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `Art 93(2) answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE      -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "sind Vor- und Zwischenentscheide nicht anfechtbar" (Art 93(2) answers for a preliminary decision in its two fields, in place of Art 93(1))
        IF `Art 93(1) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `Art 93(1) answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `Art 91 answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Art 93(1) "ist die Beschwerde zulässig: a. wenn ...; oder b. wenn ..." with neither "wenn" holding, or Art 91(a) "wenn diese Begehren unabhängig von den anderen beurteilt werden können" failing
        OTHERWISE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): each of Art 90 to 93 grants an appeal against decisions of its own kind and does not close the list of decisions that can be appealed
    WHERE
        `Art 90 answer` MEANS `Art 90 the appeal is admissible against the decision` `the decision ends the proceedings`
        `Art 91 answer` MEANS `Art 91 the appeal is admissible against the partial decision` `the decision deals with only some of the claims made` `those claims can be judged independently of the others` `the decision ends the proceedings for only some of the joint litigants`
        `Art 92(1) answer` MEANS `Art 92(1) the appeal is admissible against the preliminary or interlocutory decision on jurisdiction or recusal` `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` `the decision was notified independently` `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal`
        `Art 93(2) answer` MEANS `Art 93(2) the appeal is admissible against the preliminary or interlocutory decision in the field` `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` `the matter is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` `the matter is in the field of asylum` `the decision is on extradition detention` `the decision is on the seizure of assets or valuables` `the decision was notified independently` `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` `the decision may cause irreparable harm` `allowing the appeal would immediately bring about a final decision` `that would spare a significant expenditure of time or cost for a lengthy evidentiary procedure`
        `Art 93(1) answer` MEANS `Art 93(1) the appeal is admissible against the other preliminary or interlocutory decision` `the decision is a preliminary or interlocutory decision` `the decision was notified independently` `the decision is on jurisdiction or on a request for recusal` `the decision may cause irreparable harm` `allowing the appeal would immediately bring about a final decision` `that would spare a significant expenditure of time or cost for a lengthy evidentiary procedure`
